.\"
.\" The command table below is generated by tools/generate-manpages.py from the
.\" program's own --help output, and a test checks the two still agree.
.TH PDF-SMITHY-CLI 1 "2026" "PDF Smithy @PS_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdf-smithy-cli \- edit, merge, split, sign and OCR PDF documents from the shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdf-smithy-cli
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdf-smithy-cli
is the command-line half of PDF Smithy, and runs the same engine as the window.
Everything the graphical application can do to a document is reachable from a
script \(em that is a design rule of the project rather than a bonus, so a
workflow worked out by hand can be automated without reaching for another tool.
.PP
Nothing is uploaded anywhere. Every operation happens on the machine it is
invoked on, which is the reason the project exists.
.PP
Page ranges accept
.BR 1-4 ", " 8 ", " 12-last ", " odd ", " even
and
.BR 9-1
for reverse order, and preserve both order and repetition: 
.B --keep 1,1,2
writes the first page twice.
.PP
Coordinates are in PostScript points (1/72 inch) measured from the bottom-left
corner of the page
.I as it is shown \(em
with any rotation already applied \(em which is what a ruler held against a
viewer measures.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "info" " FILE"
Show page count, size and dimensions
.TP
.BI "merge" " FILE..."
-o OUT           Glue documents together
.TP
.BI "split" " FILE"
[-o TEMPLATE]    Break a document apart
.TP
.BI "pages" " FILE"
-o OUT           Select, reorder and rotate pages
.TP
.BI "compress" " FILE"
-o OUT           Make a document smaller
.TP
.BI "ocr" " FILE"
-o OUT           Make a scan searchable
.TP
.BI "sign" " FILE"
-o OUT           Stamp a signature image onto pages
.TP
.BI "watermark" " FILE"
-o OUT           Lay text across pages
.TP
.BI "meta" " FILE"
Show metadata; --sanitize -o OUT strips it
.TP
.BI "protect" " FILE"
-o OUT           Set or remove a password
.TP
.BI "from-images" " IMAGE... -o OUT"
Build a document from pictures
.TP
.BI "export-images" " FILE"
Render pages to image files
.TP
.BI "number" " FILE"
-o OUT           Page numbers, headers and Bates stamping
.TP
.BI "crop" " FILE"
-o OUT           Trim the empty border off pages
.TP
.BI "redact" " FILE"
-o OUT           Take content out of an area for good
.TP
.BI "nup" " FILE"
-o OUT           Put several pages on one sheet
.TP
.BI "annotate" " FILE"
List, add, remove or flatten comments
.TP
.BI "outline" " FILE"
Show or rewrite the table of contents
.TP
.BI "form" " FILE"
List, fill in or flatten form fields
.TP
.BI "text" " FILE"
Show the text of a page, or correct it
.TP
.BI "batch" " FILE..."
--out-dir DIR    Do one thing to many files
.TP
.BI "compare" " LEFT RIGHT"
Show what changed between two documents
.TP
.BI "archive" " FILE"
-o OUT           Convert to PDF/A for long-term keeping
.TP
.BI "archive-check" " FILE"
Look for what stops a file being archival
.TP
.BI "colour" " convert FILE"
Convert to grey, black and white, RGB or CMYK
.TP
.BI "colour" " coverage FILE"
Measure the total ink on each page
.TP
.BI "colour" " hairlines FILE"
Thicken strokes too thin to print
.TP
.BI "colour" " inspect FILE"
What the document does with colour
.TP
.BI "colour" " limits"
What the colour work here cannot promise
.TP
.BI "colour" " overprint FILE"
Set or clear overprint on black
.TP
.BI "colour" " replace FILE"
Swap one colour for another, everywhere
.TP
.BI "colour" " separate FILE"
Render one printing plate as an image
.TP
.BI "colour" " spot FILE"
Rename, merge or dissolve named separations
.TP
.BI "field" " add"
FILE  -o OUT      Put a new field on a page
.TP
.BI "field" " button"
FILE  -o OUT      Make a button reset, submit, jump or open a link
.TP
.BI "field" " calculate FILE"
-o OUT      Work a field's value out from other fields
.TP
.BI "field" " collect"
FILE... -o CSV    Gather many filled-in copies into one table
.TP
.BI "field" " copy"
FILE  -o OUT      Take the fields from an empty form of the same layout
.TP
.BI "field" " export"
FILE  -o DATA     Write the answers to FDF, XFDF or CSV
.TP
.BI "field" " format"
FILE  -o OUT      Show a value as a number, a date or an amount
.TP
.BI "field" " from-json FILE"
-o OUT      Build a whole form from a description
.TP
.BI "field" " import"
FILE  -o OUT      Fill the fields from FDF, XFDF or CSV
.TP
.BI "field" " limitations"
What making forms cannot promise
.TP
.BI "field" " list"
FILE              Show every field, where it sits and what it holds
.TP
.BI "field" " move"
FILE  -o OUT      Put a field somewhere else on its page
.TP
.BI "field" " remove"
FILE  -o OUT      Take fields out
.TP
.BI "field" " rename"
FILE  -o OUT      Call a field something else
.TP
.BI "field" " tab-order FILE"
-o OUT      The order the tab key walks a page
.TP
.BI "field" " update"
FILE  -o OUT      Change what a field is and how it looks
.TP
.BI "field" " validate"
FILE  -o OUT      Refuse a number outside a range
.TP
.BI "fonts" " check"
FILE                 Exit non-zero when a font is missing or unreadable
.TP
.BI "fonts" " embed"
FILE -o OUT          Add a system font, cut down to the characters asked for
.TP
.BI "fonts" " find"
FAMILY               Where this system keeps a font, if it has it
.TP
.BI "fonts" " limits"
What the font tools cannot promise
.TP
.BI "fonts" " list"
FILE                 Every font, where it is used and what is wrong with it
.TP
.BI "fonts" " merge"
FILE -o OUT          Join duplicate subsets of the same font into one
.TP
.BI "fonts" " strip"
FILE -o OUT          Throw embedded glyphs away and keep the text
.TP
.BI "fonts" " unicode"
FILE -o OUT          Write /ToUnicode maps so the text can be copied
.TP
.BI "images" " adjust FILE --resource RES"
