.BI "layout" " bleed"
FILE      -o OUT     Give the pages a bleed, growing the sheet
.TP
.BI "layout" " booklet"
FILE      -o OUT     Reorder pages into printer's spreads
.TP
.BI "layout" " boxes"
FILE                 Show the five page boxes, and which are absent
.TP
.BI "layout" " labels"
FILE                 Show the numbers the reader displays
.TP
.BI "layout" " limits"
What page layout cannot promise
.TP
.BI "layout" " marks"
FILE      -o OUT     Add printer's marks outside the trim
.TP
.BI "layout" " overlay"
BASE OVER -o OUT     Lay one document over another
.TP
.BI "layout" " poster"
FILE      -o OUT     Tile one page across several sheets
.TP
.BI "layout" " remove"
FILE      -o OUT     Take pages out
.TP
.BI "layout" " resize"
FILE      -o OUT     Put the pages on a different paper size
.TP
.BI "layout" " set-boxes"
FILE      -o OUT     Write /MediaBox, /CropBox, /BleedBox, /TrimBox, /ArtBox
.TP
.BI "layout" " set-labels FILE"
-o OUT     Write /PageLabels, e.g. i, ii, iii and then 1
.TP
.BI "layout" " split"
FILE      -o OUT     Cut each page in two, for scanned books
.TP
.BI "layout" " unify"
FILE      -o OUT     Bring every page to one size
.TP
.BI "linearise" " FILE"
[-o OUT]           Rewrite so page one arrives over a slow link first
.TP
.BI "objects" " at"
FILE --page N --at X,Y       What is under a point, topmost first
.TP
.BI "objects" " delete"
FILE --object I              Take an object off the page for good
.TP
.BI "objects" " insert"
FILE --shape S --rect R      Put text, a picture or a shape on the page
.TP
.BI "objects" " limits"
What reading and editing objects cannot reach
.TP
.BI "objects" " list"
FILE --page N|all            Everything drawn on the page, with the number to grab it by
.TP
.BI "objects" " move"
FILE --object I --by DX,DY   Shift an object across the page
.TP
.BI "objects" " restyle"
FILE --object I --fill C     Change the colours or the line width
.TP
.BI "objects" " rotate"
FILE --object I --angle DEG  Turn an object, counter-clockwise
.TP
.BI "objects" " scale"
FILE --object I --by FACTOR  Make an object larger or smaller
.TP
.BI "preflight" " FILE"
[-o OUT]         Check against a profile, and mend faults
.TP
.BI "preflight" " fixes"
Every repair and what it changes
.TP
.BI "preflight" " limitations"
What this check cannot see
.TP
.BI "preflight" " profiles"
List the profiles that ship here
.TP
.BI "preflight" " rules"
Every rule, and whether it is checked
.TP
.BI "preflight" " save-profile ID -o FILE"
