.BI "typeset" " measure"
--text T         Measure how wide text would be set
.SH OPTIONS
Run
.B pdf-smithy-cli --help
for the full list. The options each command takes are those named in its own
description above; the rest are ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Differences were found.
.B compare
and
.B archive-check
use this so that they can be read like
.BR diff (1)
in a shell condition.
.TP
.B 2
The command line could not be understood.
.TP
.B 3
The input could not be read, or part of the work was refused and reported.
.TP
.B 4
The output could not be written.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Glue two documents together:
.PP
.RS
.B pdf-smithy-cli merge a.pdf b.pdf -o both.pdf
.RE
.PP
Make a folder of scans searchable, keeping the originals:
.PP
.RS
.B pdf-smithy-cli batch scans/*.pdf --op ocr --out-dir searchable/
.RE
.PP
Take a name out of a document for good \(em removed, not covered over:
.PP
.RS
.B pdf-smithy-cli redact case.pdf --area 1:72,700,180,16 -o public.pdf
.RE
.PP
See what changed between two drafts:
.PP
.RS
.B pdf-smithy-cli compare contract-v1.pdf contract-v2.pdf
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdf-smithy (1),
.BR qpdf (1),
.BR gs (1)
